---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NativeWindowFigure from '../../components/NativeWindowFigure.astro';
import MemoryChart from '../../components/MemoryChart.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"Built-in Ad Blocking, or Full uBlock Origin | Blanc Browser"}
  description={"Blanc blocks ads and trackers from first launch, with direct site controls. Prefer uBlock Origin? Choose full uBO 1.75.0 for regular tabs on supported builds."}
  path="/features/ad-blocking"
  page="feature-ad-blocking"
  current="features"
  ogDescription={"Built-in ad and tracker blocking with direct site controls for the connection, blocked-request count, and per-site setting."}
  ogImage="/feature-ad-blocking.png"
  ogImageAlt={"Blanc's island with its site-control popover open, showing ad and tracker blocking on for the current site."}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://blanc.day/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Features", "item": "https://blanc.day/features" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Built-in ad and tracker blocking", "item": "https://blanc.day/features/ad-blocking" }
  ]
}
</script>

<main id="main-content" class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">ad blocking</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail" aria-labelledby="blocking-title">
    <h1 id="blocking-title">Ad blocking built in. uBlock Origin if you prefer it.</h1>
    <p>Blanc Blocker stops ads and known trackers with built-in lists. The shield on the Island opens its controls for the site you&rsquo;re on.</p>
  </section>

  <figure class="product-capture feature-capture">
    <NativeWindowFigure
      class="island-figure--site-controls"
      label="Blanc's Site protection popover over the Netflix website. It shows netflix.com with Blanc Blocker active, ad and tracker blocking switched on, three ads and trackers blocked on this page, and a connection that uses HTTPS."
      tone="#080706" shot="/shots/desktop/netflix.jpg" height={640}
      tab={{ url: 'https://www.netflix.com/', favicon: '/favicons/netflix.com.ico', shield: 3 }}
      dots={{ count: 4, active: 1 }}
      popover={{ host: 'netflix.com', count: 3 }}
    />
    <figcaption>The shield opens site controls for the connection, blocking state and page count. This illustration uses a sample count of three blocked requests.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="built-in-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="built-in-title">Start protected, not set up.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article>
        <h3>Built around the web, not a browser store.</h3>
        <p>Blanc Blocker loads its lists directly in the browser. You do not need to find, install, or manage an extension before browsing.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Know the site, not just the count.</h3>
        <p>Open the shield to see whether the page uses HTTPS and how many requests Blanc blocked. It reports only what the address proves, without turning the browser into a security dashboard.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Let a site through when you choose.</h3>
        <p>Need a site exception? Use the switch in the shield popover, or type <code>/allow-ads</code>. Blanc keeps the choice specific to that site instead of making it an all-or-nothing setting.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="ublock-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="ublock-title">Full uBlock Origin, not a Lite version.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article>
        <h3>Choose it from the shield.</h3>
        <p>Click the shield on the island, choose uBlock Origin, then restart Blanc to apply it. Blanc Blocker stays the default until you switch.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>The uBlock Origin you know.</h3>
        <p>Blanc includes <a href="/ublock-origin-after-chrome">uBlock Origin 1.75.0</a> with its popup, dashboard, logger, element picker, custom filters and filter-list subscriptions. Filter lists can update on their own; uBlock Origin itself updates only with reviewed Blanc releases.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Where it runs.</h3>
        <p>uBlock Origin is available for regular tabs on Apple Silicon and Intel Macs, Windows x64 and Linux x64. Private tabs always use Blanc Blocker, and so does the Intel build when it runs under Rosetta on an Apple Silicon Mac. Each profile keeps its own uBlock Origin settings, and they are not synced.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>One bundled extension, not an extension store.</h3>
        <p>uBlock Origin is the one extension Blanc includes. Blanc does not install other browser extensions.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="truth-note-title">
    <h2 id="truth-note-title">Blocking is a strong default, not a guarantee.</h2>
    <p>Blanc uses EasyList and EasyPrivacy to reduce ads and known tracking. No blocker can promise to remove every advertisement or tracker, and some sites may need an exception to work as intended.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/privacy#browsing-the-web-with-blanc">Read Blanc's network and privacy details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </aside>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--report" aria-labelledby="missed-ad-title">
    <div><h2 id="missed-ad-title">An ad got through? Send a reproducible example.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list"><article><h3>A page we can test</h3><p><a href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/issues/new?template=ad_blocking.yml">Report a missed ad</a> with its page URL, Blanc version, operating system, blocker settings, expected result and the ad you observed. A screenshot is optional. For examples containing private information, email <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:support@blanc.day">support@blanc.day</a><!--/email_off-->.</p><p>Reports help distinguish filter coverage, a blocker integration defect and an ad format the blocker does not support. A report is closed with reproduction and verification evidence, or a documented limitation.</p></article></div>
  </section>
  <MemoryChart
    headingId="blocking-memory-title"
    heading="Blocking saves memory, not just noise."
    intro="Ads and trackers cost real memory to render. With six ad-heavy sites open, blocking them at the network layer is worth gigabytes."
  />

  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="blocking-close-title">
    <h2 id="blocking-close-title">Browse with less following you around.</h2>
    <a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="ad-blocking" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
